<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3182 0 R
/E (A dependency is a using relationship. It signifies that a change in one class \(the supplier\) may affect the behavior of another class that uses it \(the client\). It is a weak, short-term, and often temporary link.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3183 0 R
/E (The most common way a dependency occurs is when a reference to one class is passed into a method of another class. The client class doesn't own the supplier class; it doesn't store it as a permanent attribute. It just uses it briefly for a single task)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
